class.description:
[AudioBusSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"audio_bus"[/code]: it stores the values that the player may change on the buses of [AudioServer], loads them when the game starts and applies them before the first sound plays (in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], right after the default bus layout is loaded and before the [SceneTree] exists, so no [AudioStreamPlayer] can start earlier).
The project's [AudioBusLayout] ([member ProjectSettings.audio/buses/default_bus_layout]) is the only source of the buses, their effects, their routing and their default values. The settings only change values on top of it:
- [b]Player buses:[/b] [member player_buses] (project setting [member ProjectSettings.settings/audio_bus/player_buses]) names the buses the player controls; if it is empty, all buses of the layout are player buses. Other buses (mix buses, sends) are never touched.
- [b]Stored values:[/b] [member store_volume], [member store_mute] and [member store_solo] (project settings [code]settings/audio_bus/store_*[/code]; volume and mute on, solo off) decide which values are saved, loaded, applied, emitted as signals and settable. A value that is not stored is not written to the file, a value of the file that is not stored (any more) is ignored, and the setter prints a warning. A stored value that a file does not have (for example after the project turned on [member store_solo]) comes from the layout.
The settings resource is an [AudioBusListSettings] with one [AudioBusSettings] entry per player bus, in the order of the layout. The defaults are the values of the layout when the game starts; the project setting [code]settings/defaults/audio_bus[/code] is not used for this domain. Buses are identified by their name ([member AudioBusSettings.bus_name]), not by their index, so a game update that adds or reorders buses keeps the stored values; buses added by an update start with their layout values. A stored player bus that the layout does not have is skipped with one warning per bus and session, and its value stays in the settings file. [AudioServer] has no stable ids for buses: a bus that a game update renames loses the player's value.
The file is [code]user://settings/audio_bus.ini[/code] by default. It holds [AudioBusSettingsRows] with one [AudioBusSettingsRow] per bus, so it can also be stored as CSV with one line per bus and one column per stored value ([member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format], or [member ProjectSettings.settings/audio_bus/format] with [member ProjectSettings.settings/audio_bus/override_format], set to [constant ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_CSV]). The output and input device are a separate domain, see [AudioDeviceSettingsServer].
All typed setters go through [method ListSettingsServer.set_entry_value] or [method ListSettingsServer.add_entry]: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] a change is applied to [AudioServer] at once and saved at the end of the frame; in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] it waits for [method SettingsServer.apply].
A new bus layout at runtime ([method AudioServer.set_bus_layout], [method AudioServer.add_bus], [method AudioServer.remove_bus], [method AudioServer.move_bus], all of which emit [signal AudioServer.bus_layout_changed]) resets the values of the buses. Once [SettingsServerManager] has started the domain, the server listens to that signal and applies the applied values ([method SettingsServer.get_applied_settings]) of the player buses again; the other buses keep the mix of the new layout. Pending changes in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] still wait for [method SettingsServer.apply]. A layout set before startup becomes the base of the defaults instead.
[b]Presets:[/b] an [AudioBusListSettings] saved in [code]res://[/code] is a preset, edited in the Inspector with a small mixer of the player buses. [method apply_preset] sets the stored values of the buses it lists; buses it does not list keep their values. [method get_current_preset] returns the preset while the values still match it; after a single change it returns [code]null[/code] and [method is_custom] returns [code]true[/code] ("Custom").
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# A volume slider from 0 to 100 %.
func _on_music_slider_value_changed(value):
	AudioBusSettingsServer.set_bus_volume_linear(&"Music", value / 100.0)

func _ready():
	$MusicSlider.value = AudioBusSettingsServer.get_bus_volume_linear(&"Music") * 100.0
	$MuteCheck.button_pressed = AudioBusSettingsServer.is_bus_mute(&"Master")

# A preset button and a "Custom" label.
func _on_night_mode_pressed():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.apply_preset(load("res://audio/night_mode.tres"))
	$PresetLabel.text = "Custom" if AudioBusSettingsServer.is_custom() else "Night mode"

# A menu with "Apply" and "Cancel".
func open_menu():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.apply_mode = SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL

func _on_apply_pressed():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.apply()

func _on_cancel_pressed():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.revert()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// A volume slider from 0 to 100 %.
private void OnMusicSliderValueChanged(double value)
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.SetBusVolumeLinear("Music", (float)(value / 100.0));
}

public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<Slider>("MusicSlider").Value = AudioBusSettingsServer.GetBusVolumeLinear("Music") * 100.0;
    GetNode<CheckBox>("MuteCheck").ButtonPressed = AudioBusSettingsServer.IsBusMute("Master");
}

// A preset button and a "Custom" label.
private void OnNightModePressed()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.ApplyPreset(GD.Load<AudioBusListSettings>("res://audio/night_mode.tres"));
    GetNode<Label>("PresetLabel").Text = AudioBusSettingsServer.IsCustom() ? "Custom" : "Night mode";
}

// A menu with "Apply" and "Cancel". Methods of the base classes are called through Singleton.
private void OpenMenu()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.ApplyMode = SettingsServer.ApplyModeEnum.Manual;
}

private void OnApplyPressed()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.Apply();
}

private void OnCancelPressed()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.Revert();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]AudioBusSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] and [ListSettingsServer] are called through [code]AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
